      "changes": {
        "status": "approved",
        "review": {
          "id": "cba3effe-6f48-4a5d-991b-19ac2fc1d603",
          "owner": "reviewer-be",
          "status": "approved",
          "verdict": "approved",
          "summary": "Behavior-preserving clean-up confirmed for T837-T839. All ten removed actingUser copies and the four inline checks (auth/rpc x3, job/rpc x1) built the identical CodeUnauthenticated/'authentication required'/AUTH_REQUIRED/nil-params error that authrpc.ActingUser now returns; differing variants (auth/rpc admin.go CodeInternal path, billing, voucher, plan, authoring, voice/spoken, modelcatalog speech) are untouched. All eleven removed writeLayout consts equal dbtime.Layout byte-for-byte, every removed formatTime normalized to UTC, every bare parseTime used RFC3339Nano, provider's inline at.UTC().Format(writeLayout) maps to dbtime.Format(at), and auth/memory/post keep their wrappers with unchanged error text. T839's newID wrappers keep the exact panic values (ids.NewHex128 returns the rand error unwrapped). A normalized line-balance check of the out-of-touches sibling files (21 for T837, 22 for T838) shows only helper renames and import additions. Reviewer re-ran gofmt -l (empty) and go vet on all 27 changed packages (pass), plus go test -count=1 on platform/dbtime, platform/ids and auth/rpc (pass). The independent Codex read-only review (gpt-6.1-sol after gpt-5.5 was rejected for the account) found no P1/P2. Two optional follow-ups only.",
          "findings": [
            {
              "priority": "P3",
              "where": "backend/internal/clip/app/speech.go:101 (T839)",
              "message": "speechID() in the same clip/app package still hand-rolls the 128-bit hex id ([16]byte, rand.Read, panic(e), hex.EncodeToString), identical to what newID() just stopped doing. Outside T839's acceptance (which names newID in service.go only); a later tidy could route it through ids.NewHex128 with panic(err) kept. modelcatalog/speech_service.go:368 speechID and provider/types.go:468 NewRecommendationID are the same shape in other contexts. (Raised by Codex and confirmed by reviewer.)"
            },
            {
              "priority": "P3",
              "where": "backend/internal/experiment/store/store.go:652, :821; experiment/store/writing_test_store.go:58, :62, :169, :221; provider/store/store.go:78, :103 (T838)",
              "message": "Inline time.Parse(time.RFC3339Nano, ...) calls remain in two of the eleven stores. They are equivalent to dbtime.Parse and acceptance only required removing the bare parseTime helpers, so not a defect; a follow-up could switch them to dbtime.Parse so the parse rule also has one owner. (Reviewer finding.)"
            }
          ],
          "commit": "fa2ee1c6216746d90432ce948bd6ea4d3db57550",
